# Strategy conventions

Authoritative reference: [`trader-pipeline.md`](mdc:docs/plans/architecture/trader-pipeline.md).
Per-strategy operator notes: `docs/strategies/*.md` (Ukrainian by operator request).

## Non-negotiables

- **Extend `BaseStrategy` from `services/strategies/base.py`.** Required
  class attributes: `strategy_type`, `name`, `description`. Required
  method: `detect(events, markets, prices)` (sync, CPU-only) OR
  `detect_async(...)` (async, I/O-bound). Pick one.
- **Use `self.create_opportunity(...)` for ID generation.** Never
  hand-construct `Opportunity` ids — `stable_id` and `id` semantics
  are non-trivial. See `agents.md` § Opportunity IDs.
- **Live prices over static.** Strategies receive a `prices` dict
  mapping token IDs to live price objects. Always prefer
  `prices[token_id]` over `market.yes_price` / `market.no_price` when
  the token id is present.
- **Decision dataclasses are fixed.** `StrategyDecision` and
  `ExitDecision` shapes live in `services/strategies/base.py`. Do
  not add fields without updating the orchestrator that consumes
  them.
- **`configure(config: dict)` maps user overrides onto `self._config`.**
  Default config dict (e.g. `NEWS_EDGE_DEFAULT_CONFIG`) is the source
  of truth for keys; the configure hook may reject unknown keys but
  must not silently typo-correct them.
- **Tests are infrastructure-level, never slug-tied.** Per
  `agents.md` § What NOT to Do: NEVER write tests bound to a specific
  strategy slug (`tail_end_carry`, etc.). Strategies are dynamic,
  DB-driven, user-definable, and may be missing across deployments.
  Test the shared base machinery, not the concrete subclass.

## LLM-touching strategies

Most strategies are zero-LLM. The exceptions (`news_edge` and any
strategy that opts into `llm_verify_trades` at the orchestrator) load
the [`ai-llm.mdc`](mdc:.cursor/rules/ai-llm.mdc) rule automatically
when `services/ai/**` or `services/news/**` paths are also in the
chat. Read it before adding LLM calls to a strategy.

## Common footguns this rule exists to prevent

- Reading `market.yes_price` while a fresh `prices[...]` is available
  — strategy decides on stale data, looks fine in tests.
- Rolling a custom `Opportunity.id` scheme — UI deduplication breaks.
- Adding a `# TODO: implement edge calc later` and shipping. This is
  a financial app — partial code causes silent losses
  (see `agents.md` § Core Principles).

